<section>
	<h2 id="styles">Styles</h2>
	<p>
		Colors, fonts, font sizes and spacing are set once in <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor &gt; Styles</strong> and used by every pattern, so a change there restyles the whole site. Open <strong>Colors</strong> to change the palette, <strong>Typography</strong> to change fonts and sizes, and <strong>Blocks</strong> to change the look of one kind of block everywhere.
	</p>

	<h3 id="style-variations">Style Variations</h3>
	<p>
		VetPress comes with four looks. Go to <strong>Appearance &gt; Editor &gt; Styles</strong>, open <strong>Browse styles</strong>, click the one you want and then <strong>Save</strong>:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Default</strong>: cobalt, butter and blush.</li>
		<li><strong>Clinic</strong>: calm ink and mint.</li>
		<li><strong>Groom Room</strong>: hot pink.</li>
		<li><strong>Night Shift</strong>: a dark look.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		A variation changes colors across the site, including the patterns you've already placed. Changes you make in Styles afterwards are added on top of the variation you picked.
	</p>

	<h3 id="section-styles">Section Styles</h3>
	<p>
		Section styles color a whole section with matching text, links and buttons, in the colors of the current variation. Select a <strong>Group</strong>, <strong>Columns</strong>, <strong>Column</strong> or <strong>Cover</strong> block and pick one under <strong>Styles</strong> in the block settings:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Bold</strong>, <strong>Bright</strong>, <strong>Soft</strong>, <strong>Soft alt</strong> and <strong>Inverse</strong> for full-width bands.</li>
		<li><strong>Card</strong>, for a group or column, makes a raised card.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3 id="block-styles">Block Styles</h3>
	<p>
		These styles give blocks the look of the clinic's paperwork. Pick them the same way, under <strong>Styles</strong> in the block settings:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Paragraph</strong>: <strong>Tag</strong> and <strong>Chip</strong>, small labels like the ones above headings and on the plan cards.</li>
		<li><strong>Heading</strong>: <strong>Label</strong>, a small heading in capitals.</li>
		<li><strong>Group</strong>: <strong>Kennel card</strong>, <strong>Staff badge</strong>, <strong>Hang tag</strong>, <strong>Timeline</strong> and <strong>Report card</strong>.</li>
		<li><strong>List</strong>: <strong>Checks</strong>, with a tick before each item, and <strong>Record fields</strong>, for label and value pairs.</li>
		<li><strong>Table</strong>: <strong>Estimate</strong>, a written estimate. Turn on the table's footer row in the block settings for the total.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		The easiest way to use them is to start from a pattern that already has them, such as <strong>Team badges</strong> for staff badges or the <strong>Service page</strong> for the estimate, and edit it.
	</p>
</section>
